1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:07,966
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:15,265 --> 00:00:16,433
<i>Dad?</i>

3
00:00:20,228 --> 00:00:23,106
<i>Billy? Sweetie?</i>

4
00:00:32,991 --> 00:00:34,200
<i>Dad…</i>

5
00:00:35,910 --> 00:00:37,829
<i>Are you leaving?</i>

6
00:00:44,627 --> 00:00:45,587
[PHONE RINGING]

7
00:00:45,670 --> 00:00:46,671
<i>Hello?</i>

8
00:00:46,755 --> 00:00:50,091
<i>Hello? What's taking you</i>
<i>so long to respond?</i>

9
00:00:50,175 --> 00:00:52,177
<i>So, can I see you tomorrow?</i>

10
00:00:52,260 --> 00:00:53,928
<i>Brandon, I'm sorry.</i>

11
00:00:54,012 --> 00:00:55,722
<i>I'm not available.</i>

12
00:00:55,805 --> 00:00:57,432
<i>You always say that.</i>

13
00:00:57,515 --> 00:00:59,476
<i>You're just making up</i>
<i>excuses at this point.</i>

14
00:00:59,559 --> 00:01:01,770
<i>What? Have you changed your mind about me?</i>

15
00:01:01,853 --> 00:01:03,938
<i>- Ma'am, it's done. Everything's installed.</i>
<i>- All done?</i>

16
00:01:04,022 --> 00:01:05,523
<i>Okay, let me check it.</i>

17
00:01:07,942 --> 00:01:10,153
<i>Okay. It's working now, sir.</i>

18
00:01:10,236 --> 00:01:11,237
<i>- Thank you.</i>
<i>- Okay.</i>

19
00:01:11,321 --> 00:01:12,614
<i>- Auntie Pres?</i>
<i>- Yes?</i>

20
00:01:12,697 --> 00:01:14,574
<i>- The CCTV cameras are done.</i>
<i>- Oh, okay.</i>

21
00:01:14,657 --> 00:01:16,284
<i>Billy, I have something to give you.</i>

22
00:01:16,367 --> 00:01:17,911
<i>- One for you, one for me.</i>
<i>- Mm-hmm.</i>

23
00:01:17,994 --> 00:01:19,245
<i>There you go.</i>

24
00:01:19,329 --> 00:01:21,623
<i>This is how you use it.</i>

25
00:01:21,706 --> 00:01:23,458
<i>- Remove this side.</i>
<i>- Mm-hmm.</i>

26
00:01:23,541 --> 00:01:24,876
<i>- Aim at their eyes.</i>
<i>- Yes.</i>

27
00:01:24,959 --> 00:01:26,461
<i>- Press it. Aim towards the bad guy.</i>
<i>- Copy.</i>

28
00:01:26,544 --> 00:01:28,671
<i>I know how to use it, Auntie. Thank you.</i>

29
00:01:28,755 --> 00:01:31,508
<i>- Okay. Here.</i>
<i>- Sorry for making you worried.</i>

30
00:01:32,133 --> 00:01:34,636
[POLICE OFFICER]
<i>You can count on us. Don't worry.</i>

31
00:01:34,719 --> 00:01:37,222
<i>We will do our best.</i>

32
00:01:38,181 --> 00:01:41,643
<i>You know, that's what you guys always say.</i>

33
00:01:42,685 --> 00:01:44,354
<i>But nothing ever happens.</i>

34
00:01:45,855 --> 00:01:47,398
<i>I'll tell the truth.</i>

35
00:01:49,567 --> 00:01:51,111
<i>That Caloy guy…</i>

36
00:01:52,320 --> 00:01:54,030
<i>He courted me before.</i>

37
00:01:54,114 --> 00:01:57,951
<i>But I turned him down.</i>

38
00:01:58,034 --> 00:02:01,371
<i>I mean, it's like he's obsessed with me.</i>

39
00:02:02,247 --> 00:02:05,291
<i>I kept rejecting him,</i>
<i>but he remained persistent.</i>

40
00:02:05,917 --> 00:02:08,670
<i>Are you saying that</i>
<i>you have nothing to do with this?</i>

41
00:02:09,796 --> 00:02:11,005
<i>Here.</i>

42
00:02:12,215 --> 00:02:14,884
<i>What's this? Where is this?</i>

43
00:02:14,968 --> 00:02:16,719
<i>I have no idea.</i>
<i>I had nothing to do with it.</i>

44
00:02:18,012 --> 00:02:20,265
<i>Billy Cariño's house.</i>

45
00:02:22,517 --> 00:02:24,102
<i>Billy's house?</i>

46
00:02:24,185 --> 00:02:27,730
<i>We won't have any peace</i>
<i>until that Billy leaves us alone!</i>

47
00:02:27,814 --> 00:02:28,898
<i>Look, if you want--</i>

48
00:02:28,982 --> 00:02:29,941
<i>Uh, Ma…</i>

49
00:02:30,942 --> 00:02:32,152
<i>What I want</i>

50
00:02:32,944 --> 00:02:34,404
<i>is for you to let me deal with Billy.</i>

51
00:02:35,155 --> 00:02:36,531
<i>I'll handle her, okay?</i>

52
00:02:36,614 --> 00:02:37,740
<i>I can do that.</i>

53
00:02:40,410 --> 00:02:41,953
[SIGHS]

54
00:02:43,997 --> 00:02:44,914
[SLAMS PALM DOWN]

55
00:02:47,208 --> 00:02:48,877
[SIGHS AGAIN]

56
00:02:54,465 --> 00:02:55,592
[SIGHS]

57
00:02:59,721 --> 00:03:01,514
Something to cool your head.

58
00:03:06,477 --> 00:03:07,604
Thanks.

59
00:03:07,687 --> 00:03:08,563
Mmm.

60
00:03:08,646 --> 00:03:12,025
[WRAPPER RUSTLING]

61
00:03:12,108 --> 00:03:18,781
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

62
00:03:23,912 --> 00:03:25,079
Thanks.

63
00:03:25,163 --> 00:03:27,165
- I needed that.
- I know, right?

64
00:03:30,835 --> 00:03:32,086
I'm sorry, dude.

65
00:03:32,754 --> 00:03:34,881
I get it.

66
00:03:35,757 --> 00:03:37,008
It's okay.

67
00:03:39,302 --> 00:03:42,388
I just don't want you to experience
what happened with my mom.

68
00:03:44,140 --> 00:03:45,475
It's been years.

69
00:03:46,851 --> 00:03:48,561
It's still a cold case.

70
00:03:52,106 --> 00:03:53,441
They still haven't caught

71
00:03:54,150 --> 00:03:55,860
the hit-and-run driver who hit her.

72
00:03:57,362 --> 00:03:59,239
That's why I want Caloy to be caught.

73
00:03:59,948 --> 00:04:01,824
And for Bea to be held accountable.

74
00:04:01,908 --> 00:04:03,284
They have to pay for what they did.

75
00:04:03,368 --> 00:04:05,578
Before they do anything else.

76
00:04:05,662 --> 00:04:12,585
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

77
00:04:25,598 --> 00:04:31,813
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

78
00:04:37,235 --> 00:04:38,444
Excuse me.

79
00:04:41,447 --> 00:04:42,824
He's here.

80
00:04:43,533 --> 00:04:45,702
Okay. Thank you, Val.

81
00:04:47,829 --> 00:04:49,330
- [SIGHS]
- [BILLY WHISPERS] Okay.

82
00:04:50,498 --> 00:04:57,046
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

83
00:05:01,384 --> 00:05:07,890
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

84
00:05:44,552 --> 00:05:48,056
[LINE RINGING]

85
00:05:48,139 --> 00:05:49,640
[PHONE RINGS]

86
00:05:49,724 --> 00:05:50,850
Hello?

87
00:05:52,310 --> 00:05:53,561
I'm here.

88
00:05:54,812 --> 00:05:56,689
Sorry, sir. Just a moment.

89
00:06:03,988 --> 00:06:05,490
[PRECIOUS] Gosh…

90
00:06:05,573 --> 00:06:09,118
Didn't I tell you yesterday
that I wasn't available?

91
00:06:09,202 --> 00:06:10,870
Why did you still come?

92
00:06:10,953 --> 00:06:13,998
Don't get mad at me
when I already told you I couldn't go.

93
00:06:14,082 --> 00:06:16,584
Why can't you just leave
Oliver to himself?

94
00:06:16,667 --> 00:06:17,752
He's not a baby.

95
00:06:17,835 --> 00:06:19,629
You just don't understand.

96
00:06:19,712 --> 00:06:20,963
Understand what?

97
00:06:21,964 --> 00:06:25,301
- That you're just leading me on?
- It's not like that, Brandon.

98
00:06:25,384 --> 00:06:27,595
You know, you just wasted my time.

99
00:06:28,221 --> 00:06:29,555
That's not true!

100
00:06:29,639 --> 00:06:31,307
If it's not true, let's go.

101
00:06:31,390 --> 00:06:34,435
- Come with me. Let's go.
- Brandon, that hurts!

102
00:06:34,519 --> 00:06:35,728
Bro.

103
00:06:36,312 --> 00:06:37,522
Bro.

104
00:06:37,605 --> 00:06:40,024
Don't force her to come
if she doesn't want to.

105
00:06:42,985 --> 00:06:44,153
You should go.

106
00:06:44,946 --> 00:06:47,281
I'll call security if you don't.

107
00:06:48,074 --> 00:06:50,284
Brandon, please just leave.

108
00:06:51,536 --> 00:06:52,578
Go on.

109
00:06:52,662 --> 00:06:59,460
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING, FADES]

110
00:06:59,544 --> 00:07:01,003
- Are you okay?
- Mm-hmm.

111
00:07:01,087 --> 00:07:02,296
Thank you.

112
00:07:02,380 --> 00:07:08,761
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING, FADES]

113
00:07:19,897 --> 00:07:22,775
I also have a background in marketing,
sales, and computer programming.

114
00:07:22,859 --> 00:07:27,196
I am certain, ma'am, that I am qualified
for the executive assistant position.

115
00:07:27,280 --> 00:07:28,990
Hmm… Okay.

116
00:07:29,073 --> 00:07:32,410
We'll consider your application
and call you.

117
00:07:32,493 --> 00:07:34,537
You may go ahead. Thank you for your time.

118
00:07:35,746 --> 00:07:37,165
All right.

119
00:07:37,248 --> 00:07:38,458
Thank you.

120
00:07:40,293 --> 00:07:43,504
[TALIA] And so, Em, I need an update
on that jewelry designer.

121
00:07:43,588 --> 00:07:46,215
- The one that I requested some time ago.
- Yes, ma'am. Okay.

122
00:07:46,299 --> 00:07:47,758
- It's really important.
- [BEA SQUEALS]

123
00:07:48,468 --> 00:07:49,969
- Hi, Ms. Talia!
- [TALIA] Ah…

124
00:07:50,553 --> 00:07:52,054
Uh… and you are?

125
00:07:52,138 --> 00:07:54,182
- Bea. Bea Mercado!
- Oh! [CHUCKLES NERVOUSLY]

126
00:07:54,265 --> 00:07:55,183
Hello!

127
00:07:55,266 --> 00:07:57,101
Good afternoon, Madam Talia!

128
00:07:57,185 --> 00:08:00,188
She's an applicant,
and she's about to leave.

129
00:08:00,271 --> 00:08:01,606
- I'm so sorry.
- You're so beautiful.

130
00:08:01,689 --> 00:08:04,108
- You're my idol! Your skin is glowing!
- This way, miss.

131
00:08:04,192 --> 00:08:06,444
- [TALIA] Okay.
- Let's go.

132
00:08:06,527 --> 00:08:07,445
Okay. Whatever.

133
00:08:07,528 --> 00:08:09,155
- [WOMAN] Go home.
- I really need that update.

134
00:08:09,238 --> 00:08:10,531
- Okay, Em?
- [BEA] Thank you.

135
00:08:10,615 --> 00:08:13,784
[TALIA] Make sure it's already prepared.
I need to know it.

136
00:08:14,702 --> 00:08:21,083
[RESOLUTE MUSIC PLAYING]

137
00:08:32,720 --> 00:08:35,139
[RESOLUTE MUSIC FADES]

138
00:08:35,223 --> 00:08:40,186
Everyone, let us welcome
the newest member of the LoveList family,

139
00:08:40,269 --> 00:08:43,272
Mr. Morrie Velasco.

140
00:08:43,356 --> 00:08:46,150
[EVERYONE]
Welcome!

141
00:08:46,234 --> 00:08:48,402
And Charm, like we talked about,

142
00:08:48,486 --> 00:08:50,780
Morrie will be joining our marketing team.

143
00:08:50,863 --> 00:08:54,075
- Yes, welcome, Morrie!
- Thank you, Ms. Charm.

144
00:08:54,158 --> 00:08:55,993
I'm so honored. I'll finally get to work

145
00:08:56,077 --> 00:08:58,162
with the award-winning team
behind the phenomenal

146
00:08:58,246 --> 00:08:59,830
Happily Ever After!

147
00:08:59,914 --> 00:09:00,957
[BLAIRE] Oh, that's nothing!

148
00:09:01,040 --> 00:09:02,667
Speaking of awards…

149
00:09:02,750 --> 00:09:05,294
Let's congratulate our chief!

150
00:09:05,378 --> 00:09:09,632
She'll receive
the Young Entrepreneur of the Year Award

151
00:09:09,715 --> 00:09:12,510
from no less than
The Philippine Business Society!

152
00:09:12,593 --> 00:09:14,470
[APPLAUSE, CHEERING]

153
00:09:14,554 --> 00:09:16,639
Thank you. That's an award for all of us.

154
00:09:16,722 --> 00:09:18,933
So, congratulations, everyone.

155
00:09:19,016 --> 00:09:20,434
Take note,

156
00:09:20,518 --> 00:09:22,937
the event is at Manila Royale Suites.

157
00:09:23,020 --> 00:09:27,233
And there's even a free hotel stay
for the awardees!

158
00:09:27,316 --> 00:09:28,317
[STAFF EXCLAIM HAPPILY]

159
00:09:28,401 --> 00:09:29,944
Chief, all of us are included, right?

160
00:09:30,027 --> 00:09:31,612
Absolutely! Let's go.

161
00:09:31,696 --> 00:09:34,907
[CHARM] OMG! What are we going to wear?

162
00:09:34,991 --> 00:09:37,159
- Let me borrow your clothes!
- Sure!

163
00:09:37,243 --> 00:09:38,119
[TONI] Will they fit her?

164
00:09:38,202 --> 00:09:40,496
I'm sure Ms. Camille is fuming.

165
00:09:40,580 --> 00:09:42,623
You got an award, and she didn't.

166
00:09:42,707 --> 00:09:46,419
Because she trusted the wrong person,
choosing Bea.

167
00:09:46,502 --> 00:09:49,672
Let's move on from that, Morrie.

168
00:09:49,755 --> 00:09:52,925
The important thing is that she
has no connection to Pebblng,

169
00:09:53,009 --> 00:09:54,760
or here in LoveList.

170
00:09:54,844 --> 00:09:58,931
So as far as this turf is concerned,

171
00:09:59,015 --> 00:10:00,600
we have nothing to worry about.

172
00:10:00,683 --> 00:10:02,643
But, chief…

173
00:10:02,727 --> 00:10:04,979
What about the home turf?

174
00:10:05,855 --> 00:10:07,565
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

175
00:10:08,149 --> 00:10:09,191
It's all good.

176
00:10:09,817 --> 00:10:12,028
Yes, don't worry about it.
Thank you, Toni.

177
00:10:15,406 --> 00:10:16,324
Okay.

178
00:10:17,575 --> 00:10:18,868
Anyway, are you ready?

179
00:10:18,951 --> 00:10:20,369
Mm-hmm. Yes.

180
00:10:20,453 --> 00:10:22,705
Charm, take care of Morrie.

181
00:10:22,788 --> 00:10:25,499
What will we wear?

182
00:10:25,583 --> 00:10:27,960
- [TONI] What should we wear?
- We should go home.

183
00:10:29,378 --> 00:10:31,422
[PRECIOUS] <i>LoveList is finally</i>
<i>back on its feet.</i>

184
00:10:31,505 --> 00:10:33,341
<i>Just focus on getting better.</i>

185
00:10:33,424 --> 00:10:37,136
<i>You're not thinking of</i>
<i>getting back at them, are you?</i>

186
00:10:38,262 --> 00:10:40,514
<i>But they've gone too far, Auntie Pres.</i>

187
00:10:43,017 --> 00:10:44,935
<i>But this will never end.</i>

188
00:10:45,770 --> 00:10:48,689
<i>If you retaliate,</i>
<i>they'll just retaliate again.</i>

189
00:10:48,773 --> 00:10:50,816
<i>Think of your brother.</i>

190
00:10:50,900 --> 00:10:53,110
<i>That's exactly why I'm worried, Auntie.</i>

191
00:10:55,780 --> 00:10:57,865
<i>They were able to break into our house.</i>

192
00:10:57,948 --> 00:10:58,991
<i>What's next?</i>

193
00:10:59,075 --> 00:11:02,036
<i>I need to stop them</i>
<i>before Oliver gets hurt.</i>

194
00:11:02,119 --> 00:11:08,834
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

195
00:11:19,678 --> 00:11:24,475
[CAR HONKING IN DISTANCE]

196
00:11:27,228 --> 00:11:33,651
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

197
00:11:44,537 --> 00:11:45,830
[CALOY] Hey!

198
00:11:48,457 --> 00:11:49,417
Caloy?!

199
00:11:53,629 --> 00:11:54,588
Well?

200
00:11:55,923 --> 00:11:56,799
What do you think?

201
00:11:57,842 --> 00:12:01,470
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES, FADES]

202
00:12:06,267 --> 00:12:07,435
[BOTTLE THUDS]

203
00:12:16,193 --> 00:12:17,194
Boss.

204
00:12:18,154 --> 00:12:19,572
I think you've had too much to drink.

205
00:12:22,324 --> 00:12:23,325
You know,

206
00:12:23,868 --> 00:12:25,161
I was young…

207
00:12:26,829 --> 00:12:28,414
when I lost my mom.

208
00:12:28,497 --> 00:12:32,126
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

209
00:12:32,209 --> 00:12:33,544
And Grandpa…

210
00:12:34,670 --> 00:12:37,173
With his condition,
I feel like I'm losing him too.

211
00:12:39,758 --> 00:12:41,051
And now Billy.

212
00:12:43,262 --> 00:12:45,639
[SIGHS] I nearly lost her.

213
00:12:46,891 --> 00:12:48,559
But she's safe, isn't she?

214
00:12:48,642 --> 00:12:50,561
But what if she hadn't been?

215
00:12:50,644 --> 00:12:52,062
Nothing will happen.

216
00:12:52,146 --> 00:12:53,689
Right?

217
00:12:53,772 --> 00:13:00,779
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

218
00:13:02,281 --> 00:13:03,532
I just realized

219
00:13:04,742 --> 00:13:06,577
how important she is to me.

220
00:13:08,454 --> 00:13:10,456
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY] I knew it.

221
00:13:11,123 --> 00:13:12,791
She's like my family.

222
00:13:13,751 --> 00:13:16,170
Her, Oliver, and Auntie Pres.

223
00:13:18,422 --> 00:13:20,341
Ever since we were in high school,

224
00:13:20,424 --> 00:13:22,092
whenever Grandpa had a gig,

225
00:13:22,968 --> 00:13:25,971
he'd leave me at Billy's house.

226
00:13:29,975 --> 00:13:33,103
<i>Dude, you're eating three pieces?!</i>
<i>Save some for the rest of us!</i>

227
00:13:33,187 --> 00:13:34,855
<i>This came from my grandpa, right?</i>

228
00:13:34,939 --> 00:13:36,607
<i>Fine. Have as much as you want.</i>

229
00:13:36,690 --> 00:13:37,816
<i>Oh, I'm sorry.</i>

230
00:13:39,735 --> 00:13:42,112
<i>- I don't like that.</i>
<i>- Oh yeah!</i>

231
00:13:42,196 --> 00:13:44,365
<i>You like the drumsticks.</i>

232
00:13:44,907 --> 00:13:49,453
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

233
00:13:49,537 --> 00:13:50,412
<i>Peace.</i>

234
00:13:51,956 --> 00:13:53,624
<i>- Fine. We're good now.</i>
- [PLATES CLATTERING]

235
00:13:53,707 --> 00:14:00,422
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

236
00:14:00,506 --> 00:14:02,883
[SINGING] <i>♪ Oh, light ♪</i>

237
00:14:02,967 --> 00:14:06,428
<i>♪ In the cold night ♪</i>

238
00:14:06,512 --> 00:14:07,346
<i>Cut!</i>

239
00:14:07,429 --> 00:14:08,556
<i>Cut, cut. Okay?</i>

240
00:14:08,639 --> 00:14:09,848
<i>Okay.</i>

241
00:14:10,641 --> 00:14:12,184
[YOUNG BILLY] <i>This is a serenade!</i>

242
00:14:12,268 --> 00:14:14,353
<i>You're singing like you're in a funeral.</i>

243
00:14:14,436 --> 00:14:15,771
<i>How could we win like that?</i>

244
00:14:15,854 --> 00:14:16,939
<i>- Again.</i>
<i>- Okay.</i>

245
00:14:17,022 --> 00:14:18,232
<i>- Do it properly.</i>
<i>- Okay.</i>

246
00:14:18,816 --> 00:14:20,234
[CLEARS THROAT] <i>Go.</i>

247
00:14:20,317 --> 00:14:22,444
[SINGING] <i>♪ Oh, light ♪</i>

248
00:14:22,528 --> 00:14:25,656
<i>♪ In the cold night ♪</i>

249
00:14:25,739 --> 00:14:30,452
<i>♪ You're like a star in the sky ♪</i>

250
00:14:31,287 --> 00:14:33,289
<i>Oh, my dear.</i>

251
00:14:33,372 --> 00:14:36,375
<i>I hope I can hear you</i>
<i>finally say yes to me.</i>

252
00:14:36,458 --> 00:14:38,502
<i>Yes, my dear.</i>

253
00:14:38,586 --> 00:14:40,337
<i>I also love you!</i>

254
00:14:40,421 --> 00:14:44,466
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

255
00:14:44,550 --> 00:14:45,593
[IN UNISON] <i>That's it!</i>

256
00:14:46,176 --> 00:14:48,470
<i>We're so good! We got it!</i>

257
00:14:49,013 --> 00:14:51,140
[GIGGLING]

258
00:14:51,223 --> 00:14:52,766
<i>- Okay, let's do it again.</i>
<i>- Okay.</i>

259
00:14:52,850 --> 00:14:54,476
<i>We'll definitely win! Okay!</i>

260
00:14:54,560 --> 00:15:00,649
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

261
00:15:01,775 --> 00:15:03,611
<i>- Wake up!</i>
<i>- What?</i>

262
00:15:03,694 --> 00:15:05,863
<i>Look, you're sleeping again!</i>

263
00:15:05,946 --> 00:15:07,072
<i>Mm!</i>

264
00:15:08,240 --> 00:15:09,950
<i>You jerk!</i>

265
00:15:10,034 --> 00:15:11,744
- [YOUNG JORDAN GRUNTS]
- [YOUNG BILLY LAUGHS]

266
00:15:11,827 --> 00:15:12,995
[GIGGLING]

267
00:15:13,078 --> 00:15:14,163
[YOUNG BILLY] <i>You jerk!</i>

268
00:15:14,246 --> 00:15:16,415
- [YOUNG BILLY GRUNTS]
- [YOUNG JORDAN LAUGHING]

269
00:15:16,498 --> 00:15:19,168
<i>Just go write there,</i>
<i>or you're going to fail.</i>

270
00:15:19,251 --> 00:15:21,837
<i>I'll tell on you to your teacher!</i>

271
00:15:21,921 --> 00:15:24,340
[BOTH GIGGLING]

272
00:15:24,423 --> 00:15:29,261
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

273
00:15:29,345 --> 00:15:30,512
[YOUNG JORDAN] <i>Dude!</i>

274
00:15:30,596 --> 00:15:31,680
<i>What?</i>

275
00:15:31,764 --> 00:15:33,182
[YOUNG JORDAN] <i>Here!</i>

276
00:15:33,265 --> 00:15:35,517
<i>- I got 85 percent!</i>
- [YOUNG BILLY CHUCKLES]

277
00:15:35,601 --> 00:15:36,852
<i>Look, I got 85!</i>

278
00:15:36,936 --> 00:15:38,812
<i>- I passed!</i>
- [YOUNG BILLY CHUCKLES]

279
00:15:38,896 --> 00:15:39,939
<i>Here!</i>

280
00:15:40,022 --> 00:15:42,149
<i>Okay, fine. Congrats.</i>

281
00:15:42,232 --> 00:15:44,902
[YOUNG BILLY] <i>But it has to be like this!</i>

282
00:15:44,985 --> 00:15:47,655
<i>I got 100 percent.</i>
[TEASING PREENING NOISE]

283
00:15:47,738 --> 00:15:49,198
[BOTH CHUCKLING]

284
00:15:49,281 --> 00:15:51,742
<i>- You're the best.</i>
<i>- I really am!</i>

285
00:15:52,409 --> 00:15:54,745
<i>Next quarter, we must both</i>
<i>score a hundred percent.</i>

286
00:15:54,828 --> 00:15:56,538
<i>You should just avoid sleeping.</i>

287
00:15:56,622 --> 00:15:58,040
<i>You always sleep in class!</i>

288
00:15:58,123 --> 00:16:00,709
<i>- Let's go inside.</i>
<i>- Close the gate!</i>

289
00:16:00,793 --> 00:16:02,670
<i>Last one in is a rotten egg!</i>

290
00:16:02,753 --> 00:16:05,172
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

291
00:16:05,255 --> 00:16:07,007
We both lost our mothers.

292
00:16:07,925 --> 00:16:09,301
We were both broken.

293
00:16:10,970 --> 00:16:12,179
But Billy…

294
00:16:14,556 --> 00:16:16,350
She used her pain

295
00:16:17,184 --> 00:16:18,477
to rise up.

296
00:16:18,560 --> 00:16:19,853
She's so strong.

297
00:16:19,937 --> 00:16:22,356
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

298
00:16:22,439 --> 00:16:24,441
She always told me,

299
00:16:24,525 --> 00:16:27,778
"Don't give up. Keep going. Go, go, go!"

300
00:16:29,697 --> 00:16:32,282
When it comes to me composing my songs,

301
00:16:32,366 --> 00:16:33,450
it's also because of her.

302
00:16:34,410 --> 00:16:36,787
You even made a new song, right?
That love song.

303
00:16:36,870 --> 00:16:38,580
[CHUCKLES]

304
00:16:38,664 --> 00:16:40,791
- Friendship song.
- Friendship song?

305
00:16:40,874 --> 00:16:43,377
- He said it's about friendship.
- Friendship song.

306
00:16:43,460 --> 00:16:48,507
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

307
00:17:06,275 --> 00:17:10,988
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

308
00:17:27,838 --> 00:17:30,257
WHERE'S OUR DESTINATION?
YOU ARE THE CAPTAIN

309
00:17:30,340 --> 00:17:32,092
I'LL RIDE YOUR WAVE WHEREVER IT TAKES ME

310
00:17:32,176 --> 00:17:34,928
DO YOU KNOW? WHEN I FOUND YOU
EVERYTHING CHANGED

311
00:17:35,012 --> 00:17:36,930
WHEREVER I GO, MY HEART WON'T BE LOST

312
00:17:37,014 --> 00:17:43,937
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

313
00:17:59,244 --> 00:18:00,120
[BEA] You…

314
00:18:00,788 --> 00:18:02,581
Why did you come here?

315
00:18:02,664 --> 00:18:04,958
Someone might recognize you.

316
00:18:05,042 --> 00:18:06,502
You know it's dangerous.

317
00:18:06,585 --> 00:18:09,713
[CHUCKLES] Even you didn't recognize me.

318
00:18:10,506 --> 00:18:11,965
Right?

319
00:18:12,049 --> 00:18:13,175
I'm pretty good, aren't I?

320
00:18:13,258 --> 00:18:15,177
[CALOY CHUCKLES] I'm really good.

321
00:18:16,220 --> 00:18:17,096
You--

322
00:18:17,846 --> 00:18:19,431
You don't have to worry.

323
00:18:19,515 --> 00:18:20,974
I checked the surroundings.

324
00:18:21,642 --> 00:18:22,935
No one was watching you.

325
00:18:23,018 --> 00:18:24,144
Just me.

326
00:18:25,062 --> 00:18:26,396
I was the only one.

327
00:18:26,980 --> 00:18:32,319
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

328
00:18:32,402 --> 00:18:34,363
[BEA EXHALES DEEPLY]

329
00:18:41,245 --> 00:18:42,246
'Bi…

330
00:18:43,622 --> 00:18:44,748
Are you okay?

331
00:18:44,832 --> 00:18:50,212
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

332
00:18:50,295 --> 00:18:51,630
[SNIFFLES]

333
00:18:55,801 --> 00:18:59,304
[SNIFFLES AGAIN]

334
00:19:00,139 --> 00:19:01,932
[SIGHS]

335
00:19:03,392 --> 00:19:09,231
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

336
00:19:11,358 --> 00:19:12,860
[SIGHS]

337
00:19:14,403 --> 00:19:16,947
[BREATHES DEEPLY]

338
00:19:17,739 --> 00:19:19,283
Caloy, I don't understand.

339
00:19:20,242 --> 00:19:23,871
I've done everything I can

340
00:19:24,663 --> 00:19:27,666
to give my mother a good life.

341
00:19:28,709 --> 00:19:29,793
[BEA SNIFFLES]

342
00:19:31,003 --> 00:19:32,337
What's happening?

343
00:19:32,963 --> 00:19:35,090
I'm back to square one.

344
00:19:35,174 --> 00:19:38,927
I want Billy's life
because it should've been mine.

345
00:19:40,012 --> 00:19:43,599
That should've been mine,
but Billy just had to steal it!

346
00:19:43,682 --> 00:19:50,147
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

347
00:20:00,657 --> 00:20:03,535
<i>I've heard so many love stories.</i>

348
00:20:03,619 --> 00:20:08,123
<i>But do you know whose love story</i>
<i>I'm most excited about?</i>

349
00:20:08,207 --> 00:20:09,041
<i>Yours.</i>

350
00:20:09,124 --> 00:20:11,460
<i>But maybe I don't really</i>
<i>have a love story.</i>

351
00:20:11,543 --> 00:20:14,963
<i>Sometimes, the best closure</i>
<i>is no closure at all.</i>

352
00:20:15,047 --> 00:20:17,132
<i>There's nothing I can do about it, right?</i>

353
00:20:17,216 --> 00:20:18,175
<i>Just use me.</i>

354
00:20:18,258 --> 00:20:19,801
<i>I'll help you.</i>

355
00:20:20,552 --> 00:20:24,014
[JORDAN] <i>Bea's mom's name</i>
<i>is Mariela Mercado.</i>

356
00:20:24,097 --> 00:20:26,975
<i>Her mother has</i>
<i>a history of mental illness.</i>

357
00:20:27,059 --> 00:20:28,810
<i>That's serious, Jordan.</i>

358
00:20:28,894 --> 00:20:31,855
<i>Maybe she really needs professional help.</i>

359
00:20:31,939 --> 00:20:34,733
[BILLY] <i>A woman has been</i>
<i>standing outside for a while now.</i>

360
00:20:34,816 --> 00:20:35,859
<i>I can't make her out clearly.</i>

361
00:20:35,943 --> 00:20:37,569
<i>- I'll check it out.</i>
<i>- No, you won't!</i>

362
00:20:37,653 --> 00:20:38,487
<i>Ma?</i>

363
00:20:39,363 --> 00:20:40,781
<i>Ma?</i>

364
00:20:43,158 --> 00:20:46,828
[MARIELA] <i>I can't bear to</i>
<i>see you suffer, my dear.</i>

365
00:20:47,746 --> 00:20:50,540
<i>Okay. Please hurry up.</i>
<i>Thank you.</i>

366
00:20:50,624 --> 00:20:52,042
<i>Why did you call the police?</i>

367
00:20:53,418 --> 00:20:55,128
<i>I didn't come here to make a scene.</i>

368
00:20:55,212 --> 00:20:57,464
<i>Billy, have mercy on me and my daughter.</i>
